1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:29,980
Transcription by CastingWords

2
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:59,980
Let's go.

3
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:09,220
Bring her into me.

4
00:02:46,041 --> 00:02:56,561
What is the deal? Why can't I fix it?

5
00:02:56,921 --> 00:02:58,901
Stop going to sleep with wet hair, idiot.

6
00:02:59,161 --> 00:03:01,221
Why won't it just work with me and lay down?

7
00:03:02,361 --> 00:03:03,901
I guess it's not that bad.

8
00:03:04,281 --> 00:03:04,761
Right.

9
00:03:05,041 --> 00:03:06,681
At least it still looks better than yours.

10
00:03:07,001 --> 00:03:07,641
What'd you say?

11
00:03:07,961 --> 00:03:08,401
Nothing.

12
00:03:08,921 --> 00:03:10,241
Come on, we're gonna be late.

13
00:03:11,001 --> 00:03:12,701
I hope they got breakfast waiting.

14
00:03:13,081 --> 00:03:13,701
I'm starving.

15
00:03:13,701 --> 00:03:15,001
Who knows with those two?

16
00:03:15,561 --> 00:03:17,341
They probably got a whole feast ready.

17
00:03:17,941 --> 00:03:20,541
More importantly, any idea what this is about?

18
00:03:21,201 --> 00:03:22,561
It's kind of early for a meeting.

19
00:03:23,261 --> 00:03:25,421
I hope there's coffee and donuts, too.

20
00:03:25,941 --> 00:03:28,381
Yeah, maybe they've got a fancy breakfast plan.

21
00:03:28,661 --> 00:03:30,021
Hey, are you guys ignoring me?

22
00:03:30,441 --> 00:03:31,261
Tell me what's up.

23
00:03:31,581 --> 00:03:33,081
Shinawa will explain soon enough.

24
00:03:33,501 --> 00:03:35,521
Until then, focus on taming your stupid hair.

25
00:03:35,901 --> 00:03:36,921
This is ridiculous.

26
00:03:37,921 --> 00:03:39,381
Why am I left in the dark?

27
00:03:45,001 --> 00:03:48,861
Hey, what's wrong?

28
00:03:48,901 --> 00:03:49,641
Why are you screaming?

29
00:03:51,201 --> 00:03:52,561
What the hell are you doing?

30
00:03:52,741 --> 00:03:55,821
How can you be so bad at cooking that you set an omelet on fire?

31
00:03:56,221 --> 00:03:59,361
I bet somebody that adding alcohol to the pan makes a tick matter.

32
00:03:59,621 --> 00:04:00,641
Is that for us?

33
00:04:00,641 --> 00:04:16,921
It's done.

34
00:04:16,921 --> 00:04:18,161
Now let's eat.

35
00:04:24,481 --> 00:04:26,601
Man, Kimizuki, this is really good.

36
00:04:27,121 --> 00:04:28,321
Where'd you learn how to cook?

37
00:04:28,721 --> 00:04:30,801
Anyone with half a brain can make an omelet.

38
00:04:30,801 --> 00:04:36,141
I would have made you a great breakfast if Mitsu hadn't been there messing things up.

39
00:04:36,261 --> 00:04:38,921
I'm telling you, flambeying is a legitimate technique.

40
00:04:39,461 --> 00:04:40,241
Don't worry.

41
00:04:40,781 --> 00:04:43,101
I'm sure you were just having an off day in the kitchen.

42
00:04:43,241 --> 00:04:44,921
You can cook us breakfast some other time.

43
00:04:45,261 --> 00:04:47,021
Keep a fire extinguisher on hand.

44
00:04:51,301 --> 00:04:53,581
So, what are we doing here, guys?

45
00:04:54,141 --> 00:04:55,981
I get the feeling that I'm being left out.

46
00:04:56,301 --> 00:04:58,701
And I thought we weren't supposed to keep secrets from each other.

47
00:05:00,801 --> 00:05:05,301
There are two things we need to discuss.

48
00:05:05,901 --> 00:05:08,941
First, that you've been the subject of some kind of human experimentation.

49
00:05:09,641 --> 00:05:12,521
And that you lost control in the heat of battle and tried to kill me.

50
00:05:13,801 --> 00:05:15,721
Second, the Lieutenant Colonel.

51
00:05:16,281 --> 00:05:18,661
Are we sure that Gurren is truly on our side?

52
00:05:18,921 --> 00:05:20,641
What do you mean, is he on our side?

53
00:05:21,121 --> 00:05:22,641
He's the one looking out for us.

54
00:05:23,061 --> 00:05:26,561
It's possible that he's been using us this whole time, specifically you.

55
00:05:27,121 --> 00:05:30,781
How did he manage to put such a powerful team together in such a short amount of time?

56
00:05:31,361 --> 00:05:34,721
It could just be that he's trying to intimidate his superiors for some reason.

57
00:05:35,121 --> 00:05:38,121
But we have to consider that there might be something bigger at stake.

58
00:05:40,441 --> 00:05:42,681
All this stuff about Gurren is news to me.

59
00:05:43,081 --> 00:05:46,561
Whatever the case, we have to decide if we're going to stick by Gurren.

60
00:05:47,301 --> 00:05:50,081
If we do, we might end up traitors to the army.

61
00:05:50,661 --> 00:05:52,361
Even if we are just following orders.

62
00:05:52,761 --> 00:05:55,801
That's why we called you here, so we can figure all this out together.

63
00:05:55,801 --> 00:06:00,561
So basically, you want to discuss the idea of abandoning the Lieutenant Colonel.

64
00:06:01,361 --> 00:06:03,241
That's one of our options, yes.

65
00:06:03,241 --> 00:06:21,301
It's blood.

66
00:06:21,801 --> 00:06:23,321
I can smell his blood.

67
00:06:25,801 --> 00:06:26,321
Blood!

68
00:06:26,321 --> 00:06:32,241
This is disgusting.

69
00:06:34,161 --> 00:06:35,241
Kura Toharagi.

70
00:06:35,881 --> 00:06:37,641
You took your time getting here.

71
00:06:37,921 --> 00:06:39,621
Is this a cursed gear experiment?

72
00:06:40,381 --> 00:06:40,821
Yes.

73
00:06:43,061 --> 00:06:47,761
I'm trying to find an efficient way to turn vampires into demons whose powers we can harness.

74
00:06:48,381 --> 00:06:50,721
Unfortunately, we're not making much in the way of progress.

75
00:06:51,441 --> 00:06:53,721
Low-level trash like these specimens are worthless.

76
00:06:54,501 --> 00:06:55,501
Dispose of them, will you?

77
00:06:55,501 --> 00:06:57,541
You didn't bring me here to kill fabs.

78
00:06:57,921 --> 00:06:59,401
Just cut to the chase already.

79
00:06:59,861 --> 00:07:01,461
Did you really come here on your own?

80
00:07:02,001 --> 00:07:03,941
Those were the orders that I received.

81
00:07:04,161 --> 00:07:06,261
You weren't afraid that I was going to kill you?

82
00:07:06,561 --> 00:07:08,141
What reason do you have to kill me?

83
00:07:08,301 --> 00:07:09,801
Because you're a cocky idiot.

84
00:07:10,221 --> 00:07:12,801
If that were the case, you'd have killed me sooner.

85
00:07:13,701 --> 00:07:16,001
Besides, you won't get rid of me while I'm of use to you.

86
00:07:21,001 --> 00:07:21,941
You've got a point.

87
00:07:22,281 --> 00:07:24,941
But that does make me wonder how useful you really are.

88
00:07:24,941 --> 00:07:27,261
And more importantly, what you've been working on lately.

89
00:07:27,781 --> 00:07:30,341
I think it's time we talk about this team you've put together.

90
00:07:31,901 --> 00:07:36,001
Yurichi Rohyakuya, Yoichi Sautome, Shihoki Mizuki.

91
00:07:36,561 --> 00:07:38,161
Where did these boys come from?

92
00:07:39,381 --> 00:07:43,361
How did you manage to find not one, but three Black Demon prospects?

93
00:07:44,081 --> 00:07:45,201
I got lucky.

94
00:07:45,801 --> 00:07:48,081
It was pure coincidence that these three recruits...

95
00:07:48,081 --> 00:07:49,461
I don't believe that for a second.

96
00:07:50,101 --> 00:07:53,401
All Black Demon prospects have been subjected to human experimentation.

97
00:07:53,401 --> 00:07:56,261
Even then, the success rate is extremely low.

98
00:07:57,821 --> 00:07:58,801
Don't get me wrong.

99
00:07:59,361 --> 00:08:02,101
I'm happy to have more Black Demon users in our ranks.

100
00:08:02,401 --> 00:08:05,701
Perhaps you should be in charge of overseeing all our Cursed Gear trials.

101
00:08:05,901 --> 00:08:07,461
Seems like a waste of my talents.

102
00:08:08,141 --> 00:08:09,781
Is that why you had me meet you out here?

103
00:08:09,781 --> 00:08:12,081
Because if that's it, I'll be on my way.

104
00:08:13,261 --> 00:08:14,441
One more question.

105
00:08:15,481 --> 00:08:18,261
What's your reason for assembling these Black Demon users?

106
00:08:19,041 --> 00:08:20,461
Are you trying to plan a coup?

107
00:08:20,461 --> 00:08:25,821
If my goal was to get rid of you, I would cut you down right where you stand.

108
00:08:26,821 --> 00:08:28,401
You wouldn't land a single blow.

109
00:08:29,121 --> 00:08:29,701
Wanna bet?

110
00:08:30,461 --> 00:08:31,881
This brings back memories.

111
00:08:33,101 --> 00:08:35,121
I didn't mean to get you so fired up.

112
00:08:35,681 --> 00:08:37,341
All in all, you're doing a good job.

113
00:08:37,341 --> 00:08:40,921
But I know your weaknesses, Gurren.

114
00:08:41,981 --> 00:08:44,021
Love, friendship, honor.

115
00:08:44,801 --> 00:08:47,601
You never learned to set aside your emotions in order to lead.

116
00:08:48,121 --> 00:08:50,801
That's something that makes you stronger and holds you back.

117
00:08:52,181 --> 00:08:54,101
And that's why I know I can trust you.

118
00:08:54,401 --> 00:08:56,081
You'll never become a threat, will you?

119
00:08:56,981 --> 00:09:01,021
I don't think someone who cares so much about his comrades is capable of betraying you.

120
00:09:01,021 --> 00:09:05,101
So, this is the part where you play the hostage card again, right?

121
00:09:05,541 --> 00:09:06,741
Who will it be this time?

122
00:09:07,141 --> 00:09:08,801
What is it that you want from me, Currito?

123
00:09:09,521 --> 00:09:11,041
Don't sound so upset.

124
00:09:13,481 --> 00:09:14,481
Tell me, Gurren.

125
00:09:15,121 --> 00:09:17,321
What do you think the future holds for all of us?

126
00:09:17,881 --> 00:09:20,921
What is the point in living in a world like this one, fighting extinction?

127
00:09:21,621 --> 00:09:23,201
I'm sure you've asked yourself that.

128
00:09:24,721 --> 00:09:26,961
Did you call me here so you could complain?

129
00:09:27,401 --> 00:09:30,841
I'm just curious to know what kind of faith you have in humanity.

130
00:09:31,701 --> 00:09:34,321
This forsaken world is almost completely devoid of hope.

131
00:09:35,021 --> 00:09:37,441
And yet you continue to build your military power.

132
00:09:38,041 --> 00:09:39,421
I want to know your intentions.

133
00:09:40,001 --> 00:09:43,161
We need more power because the world is this way, right?

134
00:09:43,401 --> 00:09:44,401
That may be true.

135
00:09:44,961 --> 00:09:49,421
But no matter how strong we are, we're as good as dead if we don't have a clear vision for the future.

136
00:09:50,041 --> 00:09:52,141
Everything we do must be for the greater good.

137
00:09:52,901 --> 00:09:53,361
You agree?

138
00:09:54,021 --> 00:09:55,561
Yeah, the greater good.

139
00:09:56,701 --> 00:09:58,781
I'm going to recover the world, Gurren.

140
00:09:58,781 --> 00:10:05,481
Since the vampires destroyed our communications network, we haven't been able to make contact with anyone outside of Japan.

141
00:10:05,881 --> 00:10:08,741
But there must be other human organizations that survived.

142
00:10:09,261 --> 00:10:09,801
I'm sure.

143
00:10:10,581 --> 00:10:12,001
So your goal is what then?

144
00:10:12,461 --> 00:10:16,061
To search for humans abroad, try and reestablish communications with them?

145
00:10:16,061 --> 00:10:17,121
No.

146
00:10:17,801 --> 00:10:21,341
My next step is to destroy every last vampire in this country.

147
00:10:21,961 --> 00:10:26,781
After that, I will systematically crush all of the remaining human organizations that are left.

148
00:10:28,461 --> 00:10:31,141
Putting the world under the demon army's control.

149
00:10:31,141 --> 00:10:33,641
I didn't know you were such a dreamer.

150
00:10:34,141 --> 00:10:35,261
Sounds like fun, right?

151
00:10:35,801 --> 00:10:36,001
Huh.

152
00:10:36,481 --> 00:10:41,301
As my opening move, I'm going to thin their ranks and exterminate all of the vampire nobles.

153
00:10:42,001 --> 00:10:43,841
You seem pretty sure of yourself.

154
00:10:44,521 --> 00:10:45,021
I am.

155
00:10:45,561 --> 00:10:50,901
There are currently 25 nobles in Japan, and I know where each of them is located at this very moment.

156
00:10:51,221 --> 00:10:53,181
If you're wrong, the army's finished.

157
00:10:53,521 --> 00:10:55,861
Then my only option is to win, right?

158
00:10:55,861 --> 00:10:58,881
How do you know your intel isn't some kind of setup?

159
00:10:59,361 --> 00:11:00,461
I've considered that.

160
00:11:00,901 --> 00:11:03,301
But we don't have time to investigate further.

161
00:11:04,041 --> 00:11:05,701
What's got you in such a hurry?

162
00:11:06,601 --> 00:11:10,501
In one month, the vampires are launching a full attack on Tokyo.

163
00:11:14,281 --> 00:11:18,141
If we continue as we are now, humanity will be crushed in an instant.

164
00:11:18,381 --> 00:11:19,561
But if we're proactive...

165
00:11:19,561 --> 00:11:21,241
We can gain the upper hand.

166
00:11:21,621 --> 00:11:22,101
Correct.

167
00:11:22,101 --> 00:11:26,441
I want you to take your team and 100 of the Moon Demon Company soldiers to Nagoya.

168
00:11:27,001 --> 00:11:29,681
There, you'll find a base that houses 10 vampire nobles.

169
00:11:30,241 --> 00:11:32,121
Kill all of them and claim the facility.

170
00:11:32,801 --> 00:11:35,061
If we attack, they'll realize what you're planning.

171
00:11:35,401 --> 00:11:35,801
Perhaps.

172
00:11:36,481 --> 00:11:39,061
But it'll be worth it if we can distract them for a while.

173
00:11:39,461 --> 00:11:41,641
In the meantime, we'll prepare for the final battle.

174
00:11:42,901 --> 00:11:44,361
So, we're disposable.

175
00:11:45,581 --> 00:11:47,861
This is a very important mission, Gurren.

176
00:11:48,341 --> 00:11:51,021
I've come to you because I need someone that I can trust.

177
00:11:51,021 --> 00:11:54,661
If you can accomplish this task, I can take over from there.

178
00:11:54,981 --> 00:11:58,581
So what you're actually saying is that you don't want to tell me your whole plan right now.

179
00:11:58,861 --> 00:12:00,301
And I thought you trusted me.

180
00:12:05,661 --> 00:12:06,541
Your directive.

181
00:12:06,541 --> 00:12:19,161
Go, that's an order, not a request.

182
00:12:20,301 --> 00:12:21,041
Just wait.

183
00:12:21,881 --> 00:12:25,561
I'm going to show you a world where it's the vampires who serve as our livestock.

184
00:12:25,561 --> 00:12:38,681
Don't be fooled, my love.

185
00:12:39,421 --> 00:12:41,881
It's my orders that you're supposed to be following.

186
00:12:42,941 --> 00:12:46,681
Remember, I'm the only one who can make your wish come true.

187
00:12:47,141 --> 00:12:47,821
Shut up.

188
00:12:47,821 --> 00:13:14,181
Let me guess.

189
00:13:14,181 --> 00:13:16,421
You've spotted some girl taking off her clothes.

190
00:13:16,561 --> 00:13:19,061
How come you always assume I'm doing something perverted?

191
00:13:19,321 --> 00:13:21,401
Why else would you be staring so intently?

192
00:13:23,521 --> 00:13:24,701
Is it true what you said?

193
00:13:25,401 --> 00:13:27,281
Did I really almost kill you, Shinoa?

194
00:13:28,441 --> 00:13:29,121
Well, yeah.

195
00:13:29,201 --> 00:13:31,781
But the nice thing is you didn't actually go through with it in the end.

196
00:13:33,641 --> 00:13:36,281
Whatever your intentions were, I'm still alive and kicking.

197
00:13:36,801 --> 00:13:38,541
Try not to beat yourself up about it.

198
00:13:38,541 --> 00:13:40,601
We'll figure out what's going on.

199
00:13:41,681 --> 00:13:45,221
But normally, I would spend the entire fight protecting you.

200
00:13:45,361 --> 00:13:49,321
Oh, I'm glad to hear you've finally figured out your role in our team's formation.

201
00:13:50,041 --> 00:13:54,821
You and Kamizuki, you guys are like the linemen, the strong knights of Shinoa's squad.

202
00:13:55,061 --> 00:13:59,421
Your job is to protect the queen and lay down your lives to ensure my safety.

203
00:14:01,621 --> 00:14:02,381
Hey, you?

204
00:14:02,381 --> 00:14:05,681
Did Gurren plan on me losing control?

205
00:14:06,321 --> 00:14:08,101
Was that what he was going for the whole time?

206
00:14:08,621 --> 00:14:09,021
Probably.

207
00:14:10,021 --> 00:14:12,821
I understand if you haven't made up your mind yet.

208
00:14:13,401 --> 00:14:14,781
I was looking to the west.

209
00:14:15,321 --> 00:14:15,541
Huh?

210
00:14:16,641 --> 00:14:21,361
Hey, the next time we're up against those bloodsuckers, will you promise to stay by my side?

211
00:14:21,621 --> 00:14:23,421
What's gotten into you all of a sudden?

212
00:14:24,561 --> 00:14:27,461
Well, if I lose control, you can stop me, but...

213
00:14:27,461 --> 00:14:29,501
We'll make sure nothing bad happens to you.

214
00:14:31,161 --> 00:14:32,061
Thanks, Shinoa.

215
00:14:34,921 --> 00:14:37,181
I'm just doing my job as the squad's leader.

216
00:14:38,141 --> 00:14:40,181
Don't worry. We're in this together.

217
00:14:40,561 --> 00:14:41,241
I know that.

218
00:14:42,601 --> 00:14:44,381
All right. We should go back.

219
00:14:45,481 --> 00:14:48,161
The others are probably mad that I've taken so long up here.

220
00:14:48,161 --> 00:14:58,041
I've decided I'm going to stick with Gurren.

221
00:14:59,441 --> 00:15:02,241
Family. That's what he's called our team from the very beginning.

222
00:15:02,961 --> 00:15:03,381
Mitsuba.

223
00:15:04,461 --> 00:15:04,861
Yoichi.

224
00:15:05,961 --> 00:15:06,501
Kimizuki.

225
00:15:07,561 --> 00:15:08,041
Shinoa.

226
00:15:08,841 --> 00:15:10,541
You're my new brothers and sisters.

227
00:15:12,141 --> 00:15:13,521
I really believe that.

228
00:15:14,041 --> 00:15:15,461
You're all important to me.

229
00:15:15,461 --> 00:15:16,461
But...

230
00:15:16,461 --> 00:15:19,401
I can't forget about Mika either.

231
00:15:20,001 --> 00:15:22,021
He's also an important member of my family.

232
00:15:23,581 --> 00:15:27,761
My parents abandoned me, so I never really learned how families are supposed to work.

233
00:15:28,401 --> 00:15:28,461
But...

234
00:15:29,461 --> 00:15:33,701
I'm pretty sure you don't turn your back on your brother just because he kept a secret from you.

235
00:15:34,641 --> 00:15:37,401
Gurren said he'd help me get Mika back and complete my family.

236
00:15:38,101 --> 00:15:39,581
I'm going to trust his word.

237
00:15:39,581 --> 00:15:44,641
I know I have no right to get you all involved in personal issues like this.

238
00:15:45,461 --> 00:15:47,421
If you want me to leave...

239
00:15:47,421 --> 00:15:48,001
I've heard enough.

240
00:15:53,341 --> 00:15:56,061
You were right when you said you can't turn your back on family.

241
00:15:56,521 --> 00:15:56,941
Agreed?

242
00:15:59,341 --> 00:15:59,821
Yeah.

243
00:15:59,821 --> 00:16:14,421
Well, it sounds like we've reached a conclusion.

244
00:16:15,101 --> 00:16:16,401
We defend our family.

245
00:16:17,061 --> 00:16:21,861
In this messed up world, most people are so busy trying to survive that they forget to look out for each other.

246
00:16:21,861 --> 00:16:26,641
But Shinoa's squad is different.

247
00:16:26,881 --> 00:16:28,781
You can probably thank my strong leadership.

248
00:16:30,401 --> 00:16:32,821
Now, if we could just do something about our teammates' hair.

249
00:16:33,061 --> 00:16:33,201
What?

250
00:16:33,341 --> 00:16:34,601
Hey, shut up!

251
00:16:34,601 --> 00:16:34,981
Mika!

252
00:16:34,981 --> 00:16:52,741
Oh, you're here.

253
00:16:53,201 --> 00:16:55,121
I was just getting some blood ready.

254
00:16:55,121 --> 00:17:02,501
Are you really that thirsty?

255
00:17:03,461 --> 00:17:04,341
There, there.

256
00:17:04,541 --> 00:17:05,941
Drink your fill, my pet.

257
00:17:11,861 --> 00:17:13,101
I'm sorry, Cruel.

258
00:17:13,561 --> 00:17:16,521
We all get a little ravenous when we haven't had enough blood.

259
00:17:17,081 --> 00:17:19,581
Um, can you give me a little extra?

260
00:17:20,161 --> 00:17:21,861
Of the serum, I mean.

261
00:17:21,861 --> 00:17:24,761
Oh, I can give you as much as you want.

262
00:17:28,881 --> 00:17:32,341
But you know, you won't last forever on my blood alone.

263
00:17:34,261 --> 00:17:36,961
The day will come when you'll have to drink from a human.

264
00:17:38,321 --> 00:17:39,441
Wait outside for now.

265
00:17:39,861 --> 00:17:41,041
I'll send for you when I'm dying.

266
00:17:41,861 --> 00:17:42,261
Right.

267
00:17:50,861 --> 00:17:51,301
Hmm.

268
00:17:51,861 --> 00:17:53,261
Was there something else?

269
00:17:53,381 --> 00:17:55,401
You were supposed to kill Yuichiro and me.

270
00:17:55,821 --> 00:17:57,901
So what are you playing at by letting us live?

271
00:17:58,241 --> 00:17:59,661
You sound so serious.

272
00:17:59,981 --> 00:18:02,341
Don't tell me you're worried about my safety, Mika.

273
00:18:02,881 --> 00:18:05,161
Why would you put yourself at risk to save us?

274
00:18:05,821 --> 00:18:07,741
It just doesn't make any sense to me.

275
00:18:09,001 --> 00:18:10,841
What are you planning on doing with you?

276
00:18:11,161 --> 00:18:11,781
And with me?

277
00:18:12,261 --> 00:18:13,021
Oh, Mika.

278
00:18:13,521 --> 00:18:15,841
That's information I'd rather keep to myself.

279
00:18:16,041 --> 00:18:17,001
Don't mess with me!

280
00:18:17,741 --> 00:18:21,021
If you're gonna end up hurting you, then I'll put a stop to this right now!

281
00:18:21,021 --> 00:18:23,601
How exactly?

282
00:18:25,061 --> 00:18:27,481
After all, you're just my little pet, remember?

283
00:18:27,481 --> 00:18:29,341
Stop it.

284
00:18:29,761 --> 00:18:31,241
I can't do this anymore.

285
00:18:31,861 --> 00:18:32,601
Come on.

286
00:18:32,821 --> 00:18:34,161
Now you're just being dramatic.

287
00:18:34,821 --> 00:18:37,641
Eventually you'll realize the vampires aren't as bad as the humans.

288
00:18:38,121 --> 00:18:38,921
It's for the better.

289
00:18:38,921 --> 00:18:40,401
I like you and your old friend.

290
00:18:40,661 --> 00:18:42,361
You expect me to believe that?

291
00:18:43,361 --> 00:18:44,541
Without question.

292
00:18:47,741 --> 00:18:48,221
Fine.

293
00:18:48,221 --> 00:18:52,781
If you're going to start sulking, then I'll tell you why I've kept the two of you alive.

294
00:18:52,781 --> 00:18:57,441
And why I require the power of the Seraph of the End for myself.

295
00:18:57,441 --> 00:19:10,801
Next month, we're attacking the humans again.

296
00:19:11,361 --> 00:19:15,881
This time we'll send in our strongest units and we won't stop until every one of them is dead.

297
00:19:15,881 --> 00:19:19,981
This will be the final battle between humans and vampires.

298
00:19:20,901 --> 00:19:26,381
In order to save you, you're gonna have to go undercover and hide from both sides of this war.

299
00:19:26,861 --> 00:19:28,381
I'm giving you a secret mission.

300
00:19:29,361 --> 00:19:34,601
And if you fail, then you'll be a traitor to both sides and the whole world will turn on you.

301
00:19:34,601 --> 00:19:37,121
I understand.

302
00:19:37,781 --> 00:19:39,681
I'll save you from the vampires.

303
00:19:40,401 --> 00:19:42,161
And from the humans as well.

304
00:19:51,241 --> 00:19:52,041
Come in.

305
00:19:55,001 --> 00:19:56,061
Excuse me, sir.

306
00:19:58,381 --> 00:20:01,901
I thought you'd like to know that you and Komizuki have completed their training.

307
00:20:01,901 --> 00:20:05,121
They have both succeeded in possession.

308
00:20:05,421 --> 00:20:05,941
Impressive.

309
00:20:06,261 --> 00:20:06,701
Indeed.

310
00:20:09,361 --> 00:20:11,901
Last time we talked, you had a question for me.

311
00:20:12,301 --> 00:20:13,961
You asked if I'd fallen for you.

312
00:20:14,461 --> 00:20:16,341
I don't remember prying like that.

313
00:20:17,041 --> 00:20:17,841
What's your answer?

314
00:20:18,821 --> 00:20:20,781
I'm honestly not sure myself.

315
00:20:21,541 --> 00:20:24,801
It's just, for the first time in my life, someone needs me.

316
00:20:25,061 --> 00:20:27,401
And I can't let him down when he's counting on me.

317
00:20:30,801 --> 00:20:31,721
All right, then.

318
00:20:31,901 --> 00:20:33,321
I'll see myself out.

319
00:20:34,041 --> 00:20:34,801
Hold on.

320
00:20:35,081 --> 00:20:36,421
I've got a new mission for you.

321
00:20:36,941 --> 00:20:39,781
Come to the staging arena tomorrow at 0600 hours.

322
00:20:42,941 --> 00:20:45,581
We're going to kill all the vampires in Nagaya.

323
00:20:45,581 --> 00:20:59,881
Looks like he got the order, too.

324
00:21:00,221 --> 00:21:02,801
We've been instructed to move our main units to Nagaya.

325
00:21:02,801 --> 00:21:04,801
We'll hit Tokyo soon after that.

326
00:21:04,801 --> 00:21:05,761
Yes, I know.

327
00:21:12,601 --> 00:21:14,581
Increased sensitivity on the left side.

328
00:21:14,761 --> 00:21:15,381
Roger that.

329
00:21:15,381 --> 00:21:22,301
The preparation is complete, Lieutenant General Kuretto.

330
00:21:23,061 --> 00:21:23,561
Begin.

331
00:21:23,561 --> 00:21:38,521
Increase the power.

332
00:21:38,521 --> 00:21:39,021
Higher.

333
00:21:39,021 --> 00:21:50,201
But, sir, if we go higher, it's likely she'll die.

334
00:21:50,201 --> 00:21:51,821
Do it.

335
00:21:52,461 --> 00:21:53,141
That's good.

336
00:21:53,141 --> 00:21:53,241
arently.

337
00:21:57,461 --> 00:21:57,661
That's true, bro.

338
00:21:57,661 --> 00:21:58,241
Great news

339
00:21:58,241 --> 00:21:59,501
and now.

340
00:21:59,981 --> 00:22:01,161
We'll see you next time in Nagaya.

341
00:22:01,581 --> 00:22:01,961
All right, Rebecca.

342
00:22:01,961 --> 00:22:02,501
Thanks for having me on the left side.

343
00:22:02,881 --> 00:22:03,101
Thank you, Rick.

344
00:22:07,441 --> 00:22:08,061
redo it.

345
00:23:25,029 --> 00:23:34,889
Next time on Seraph of the End, the Moon Demon's Orders.

